 <section class="panel" id="finder-search" aria-label="Search options"><h2>Find your next activation</h2><div class="searchline"><label for="place">Town, city, state, ZIP or reference number</label><div class="inputrow"><input id="place" placeholder="e.g. Glasgow, KY or W4K/EC-001" autocomplete="off"><button id="town" class="primary">Search</button><button id="gps" class="secondary">◎ Use GPS</button></div></div><p class="meta searchtip">Tip: search a <b>town, city or ZIP</b> to see many parks nearby. Search a <b>reference number</b> (like US-1234 or W4K/EC-001) to see just that one park, then use “Show nearby parks” to widen it.</p><div class="filters"><fieldset><legend>Programs</legend><label><input id="sota" type="checkbox" checked> SOTA</label><label><input id="pota" type="checkbox" checked> POTA</label><label><input id="wwff" type="checkbox" checked> WWFF</label></fieldset><label class="radius">Search radius<select id="radius"><option value="25">25 miles</option><option value="50" selected>50 miles</option><option value="100">100 miles</option><option value="200">200 miles</option><option value="500">500 miles</option></select></label></div><p id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading location records…</p><div id="km-bar" style="margin-top:12px"></div><details class="layerdrop"><summary><span>🗺️ Park boundaries</span><span class="drophint">tap to show/hide layers</span></summary><div class="gis-group"><strong>Official park boundaries (Kentucky)</strong><div class="gis-row"><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-bstate" type="checkbox" checked><i style="background:#2fa84f"></i>State Parks</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-bwma" type="checkbox" checked><i style="background:#f08a1c"></i>WMAs &amp; hunting areas</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-bsnp" type="checkbox" checked><i style="background:#a25ee0"></i>Nature preserves</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-bsna" type="checkbox" checked><i style="background:#e2559f"></i>Natural areas</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-bdbnf" type="checkbox" checked><i style="background:#2f7fd6"></i>Daniel Boone NF</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-bnps" type="checkbox" checked><i style="background:#9b6a3c"></i>National Park Service</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-bwild" type="checkbox" checked><i style="background:#16b3c0"></i>Wild River corridors</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-bwilder" type="checkbox" checked><i style="background:#c6e03a"></i>Wilderness areas (Clifty)</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-bfws" type="checkbox" checked><i style="background:#5ab0ff"></i>Wildlife refuges &amp; fish hatcheries</label><p class="gis-note" style="flex-basis:100%;margin:2px 0 6px;font-weight:700"><span style="display:inline-block;width:22px;border-top:3px dotted #ff2a2a;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:6px"></span>Red dotted outline = other government land (tap it to see what it is).</p><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-busace" type="checkbox" checked><i style="background:transparent;border:2px solid #ff8c38"></i>Army Corps of Engineers land (orange outline, usually not POTA)</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-bpad" type="checkbox" checked><i style="background:#e8b04a"></i>More official outlines (USGS PAD-US)</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-bkpc" type="checkbox" checked><i style="background:#ffd400"></i>OpenStreetMap outlines (unofficial)</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-ntrails" type="checkbox" checked><i style="background:linear-gradient(90deg,#ff5fa2 50%,#ffb347 50%)"></i>Other states: national trails (POTA): pink = scenic, orange dashes = historic. Kentucky uses the trail layers below.</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-padus" type="checkbox" checked><i style="background:linear-gradient(90deg,#ffd633 50%,#38e8ff 50%)"></i>Other states: official land (USGS PAD-US): gold = federal, blue = state, orange = Army Corps (usually not POTA). Zoom in to county level. Kentucky uses the layers above.</label></div><p id="gis-bstatus" class="gis-note" aria-live="polite">Choose a boundary layer to show official park boundaries. Tap a boundary for its POTA reference and official map.</p></div></details><details class="layerdrop"><summary><span>🥾 Trails · campgrounds · lodges</span><span class="drophint">tap to show/hide layers</span></summary><div class="gis-group"><strong>Official GIS trails</strong><div class="gis-row"><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-tears" type="checkbox" checked><i style="background:#ef8a98"></i>Trail of Tears (NPS)</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-lewis" type="checkbox" checked><i style="background:#5bd5ec"></i>Lewis &amp; Clark (NPS)</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-lewisauto" type="checkbox"><i style="background:#2f9fb8"></i>Lewis &amp; Clark auto tour route (signed roads)</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-pine" type="checkbox" checked><i style="background:#ffc36b"></i>Pine Mountain Trail (full)</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-dawkins" type="checkbox" checked><i style="background:#c7a5ff"></i>Dawkins Line (full)</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-sheltowee" type="checkbox" checked><i style="background:#6cdb97"></i>Sheltowee Trace (full trail)</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-stateparks" type="checkbox"><i style="background:#e2c76b"></i>State park trails</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-trailheads" type="checkbox"><i style="background:#f5b45d"></i>Trailheads</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-camping" type="checkbox"><i style="background:#a5de9b"></i>Campgrounds</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-campsites" type="checkbox"><i style="background:#7fd3c4"></i>Campsites (zoom in)</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-lodges" type="checkbox"><i style="background:#ff9f7a"></i>Lodges</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-cottages" type="checkbox"><i style="background:#f2a6c8"></i>Cottages</label><label class="gis-cb"><input id="gis-infosites" type="checkbox"><i style="background:#f4f1e8"></i>Park offices &amp; info</label></div><p id="gis-status" class="gis-note" aria-live="polite">Choose a trail. Sheltowee, Pine Mountain and Dawkins show the full official trail statewide; the others load for the area on the map (zoom level 8+) and update as you move.</p><button id="gis-load" type="button" class="gis-btn">Reload trails</button><p class="gis-note">POTA-to-trail proximity results use distances from POTA reference coordinates to the mapped route, <strong>not official park-boundary intersections</strong>. A historic trail line may be approximate, on water, inaccessible, or on private land. Verify program rules, access and boundaries independently.</p><div id="gis-candidates" style="max-height:240px;overflow:auto;font-size:.87rem"></div></details></section><div class="mapgrid"><section class="panel mapwrap" id="finder-map" aria-label="Map"><div class="map-legend" role="group" aria-label="Map marker color legend"><strong>Map Pin Legend</strong><div class="map-legend-items"><span><i class="legend-dot legend-pota" aria-hidden="true"></i> POTA Parks</span><span><i class="legend-dot legend-sota" aria-hidden="true"></i> SOTA Summits</span><span><i class="legend-dot legend-wwff" aria-hidden="true"></i> WWFF / KFF</span></div></div><div id="map" aria-label="Interactive location map"></div><button id="gis-inside-btn" type="button" class="gis-btn gis-btn-big">📍 Am I inside a park?</button><div id="gis-inside" aria-live="polite" class="gis-inside"></div><p data-gis="bstatus" class="gis-note" aria-live="polite">Turn on a boundary layer under 🗂️ Map layers above the map to show official park boundaries. Tap a boundary for its POTA reference and official map.</p><p data-gis="status" class="gis-note" aria-live="polite">Turn on a trail layer under 🗂️ Map layers above the map. Sheltowee, Pine Mountain and Dawkins show the full official trail statewide; others load for the area on the map (zoom level 8+) and update as you move.</p><div data-gis="candidates" style="max-height:240px;overflow:auto;font-size:.87rem"></div><p class="footnote">Map markers show supplied reference coordinates, not official activation boundaries. Always verify eligibility, access, and safety before operating.</p></section><section class="panel resultssec" id="finder-results" aria-label="Nearby locations"><div class="resultshead"><h2>Nearby locations</h2><span id="count">—</span></div><p class="meta listnote">Tap a pin for park info. Official map links appear on selected POTA parks; they don’t confirm POTA eligibility.</p><div id="items"><p class="empty">Choose GPS or search for a town to begin.</p></div></section></div><section id="finder-planner" class="planner panel" aria-label="Saved activation locations"><div class="plannerhead"><h2>Activation planner</h2><button id="clearplan" class="secondary" type="button">Clear trip</button></div><p class="meta">Save parks or summits from your search results. Favorites and trip stops stay in this browser.</p><div class="plannercols"><div><h3>Favorites <span id="favcount">0</span></h3><div id="favorites"></div></div><div><h3>Trip stops <span id="tripcount">0</span></h3><div id="tripstops"></div><a id="triproute" class="routebtn" href="#" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" hidden>Open trip in Google Maps</a></div></div></section><section class="panel" aria-label="Cross-program planning"><h2>Cross-program activation opportunities</h2><p class="meta">Some POTA results show WWFF reference matches from a January 2025 cross-reference. These are <strong>historical reference matches only</strong>; they do not confirm that you can activate more than one program at the same time. Being near a summit or park does not confirm SOTA/POTA/WWFF eligibility. Before activating, check current official boundaries, access, and each program’s rules.</p></section><section class="panel" id="finder-about" aria-label="About this map and offline notes"><h2>About this map &amp; offline use</h2><div class="gis-notice panel-notice" role="note"><b>Built for Kentucky.</b> The park boundaries, trails and “Am I inside a park?” check cover Kentucky only for now. Searching and park pins work nationwide, and overlays for other states may be added later.<br><b>A planning tool, not the final word.</b> GIS lines can be simplified, out of date or different from what POTA uses, and a boundary on this map doesn’t confirm POTA eligibility, public access or current rules. Before you activate, check the managing agency’s official map, the park’s POTA page, posted rules and closures, and hunting seasons. When in doubt, ask the land manager.<details class="gis-missing"><summary>Parks with an OpenStreetMap outline (unofficial) or no boundary</summary><p><b>OpenStreetMap outlines (unofficial)</b> (yellow dash-dot, no shading, under <i>OpenStreetMap outlines (unofficial)</i>): no official boundary file exists for these, so the outline is traced from OpenStreetMap. Check the park’s own map before you set up.</p><ul><li><a href="https://pota.app/#/park/US-3802" target="_blank" rel="noopener">US-3802</a> Clyde E. Buckley Sanctuary</li><li><a href="https://pota.app/#/park/US-10173" target="_blank" rel="noopener">US-10173</a> Kentucky Horse Park</li><li><a href="https://pota.app/#/park/US-1264" target="_blank" rel="noopener">US-1264</a> Levi Jackson Wilderness Road Park</li><li><a href="https://pota.app/#/park/US-3787" target="_blank" rel="noopener">US-3787</a> White Hall State Historic Site</li><li><a href="https://pota.app/#/park/US-3789" target="_blank" rel="noopener">US-3789</a> William Whitley House State Historic Site</li></ul><p><b>Pin only, no outline yet:</b></p><ul><li><a href="https://pota.app/#/park/US-10172" target="_blank" rel="noopener">US-10172</a> Salato Wildlife Refuge</li></ul><p><b>Official U.S. Fish &amp; Wildlife land</b> (light blue, under <i>Wildlife refuges &amp; fish hatcheries</i>): Green River NWR, Clarks River NWR, Reelfoot NWR, Ohio River Islands NWR and Wolf Creek National Fish Hatchery.</p><p><b>Shown as trail lines, not boundaries:</b> Sheltowee Trace (US-11181), Pine Mountain State Scenic Trail (US-10102), Dawkins Line (US-1253), Trail of Tears (US-3791) and Lewis &amp; Clark (US-4572). For trail parks you must be on the trail itself.</p><p><b>Inside a larger boundary:</b> Clifty Wilderness (US-3801) sits within Daniel Boone National Forest — turn on <i>Wilderness areas</i> to see its own boundary in lime green.</p></details></div></section><section id="finder-tools" class="panel tools" aria-label="Export and sharing"><h2>Field tools</h2><p class="meta">Download a CSV of your search results for offline reference, or share the current location search. Saved trip stops can also be exported.</p><div class="toolbuttons"><button id="exportresults" class="secondary" type="button">Download search results (CSV)</button><button id="exporttrip" class="secondary" type="button">Download trip (CSV)</button><button id="sharesearch" class="secondary" type="button">Share search</button></div><p class="meta">CSV files contain reference coordinates, not park boundaries or access permission.</p></section><section class="panel" id="trailfinder" aria-label="Historic and recreation trail planning"><h2>Trails &amp; Nearby Activations</h2><p class="meta">Explore five major Kentucky trails and search for SOTA, POTA and WWFF locations near a trail town or access point. Historic route lines are not necessarily walkable trails or eligible activation areas.</p><aside class="trailnotice" role="note" aria-label="Trail information notice"><strong>Trail Information Notice:</strong> Trail information is currently limited and does not include every hiking, recreational, or historic trail in the United States. Additional trails and mapping data may be added as they become available. Always verify trail routes, access, closures, and activation eligibility with official sources before traveling.</aside><aside class="notice kpc-overlap-notice" role="note">Please read: this is a research aid, not a ruling. The Park Overlap Finder shows places where our maps suggest the boundaries of two or more POTA parks may overlap. It is a starting point for your own research only. The Kentucky Portable Club cannot confirm or deny that any location listed here is a valid multi-park activation site. Park boundaries change, maps can be out of date or imprecise, and private land, closures and local rules may apply even inside a boundary. Before you count an activation, check each park&#39;s official boundary map from the managing agency, make sure you are on public land that is open to the public, and follow POTA&#39;s activation rules. POTA makes the final decision on every activation, not KPC. You are responsible for confirming your own location. KPC is an independent ham radio club, not part of Parks on the Air®.</aside><div class="trailgrid"><article class="trailcard"><h3>Sheltowee Trace</h3><p>Kentucky and Tennessee recreation trail. Check current trail conditions and reroutes before hiking.</p><div class="links"><a href="https://sheltoweetrace.org/maps" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Trail maps &amp; updates ↗</a></div><button type="button" class="secondary trailsearch" data-town="Morehead, KY">Search near Morehead, KY</button><button type="button" class="secondary trailsearch" data-town="Stearns, KY">Search near Stearns, KY</button></article><article class="trailcard"><h3>Trail of Tears</h3><p>National historic trail: multiple historical routes and visitor sites, not one continuous hiking path.</p><div class="links"><a href="https://www.nps.gov/trte/planyourvisit/maps.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NPS visitor map ↗</a><a href="https://irmadev.nps.gov/DataStore/Reference/Profile/2238914" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NPS route GIS ↗</a></div><button type="button" class="secondary trailsearch" data-town="Hopkinsville, KY">Search near Hopkinsville, KY</button></article><article class="trailcard"><h3>Lewis &amp; Clark</h3><p>National historic trail with river and historic alignments; separate from the visitor driving route.</p><div class="links"><a href="https://www.nps.gov/lecl/planyourvisit/maps.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NPS trail maps ↗</a><a href="https://www.lewisclarkcorridors.org/maps/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Route GeoJSON source ↗</a></div><button type="button" class="secondary trailsearch" data-town="Paducah, KY">Search near Paducah, KY</button></article><article class="trailcard"><h3>Pine Mountain State Scenic Trail</h3><p>State-managed trail with distinct hiking sections; verify the open section and access before visiting.</p><div class="links"><a href="https://parks.ky.gov/parks/find-a-park/pine-mountain-state-scenic-trail-7826" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Kentucky State Parks section maps, shelters &amp; access ↗</a></div><button type="button" class="secondary trailsearch" data-town="Whitesburg, KY">Search near Whitesburg, KY</button></article><article class="trailcard"><h3>Dawkins Line Rail Trail</h3><p>State rail trail with designated parking and current access advisories.</p><div class="links"><a href="https://parks.ky.gov/explore/dawkins-line-rail-trail-7831" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official map, trailheads &amp; access alerts ↗</a></div><button type="button" class="secondary trailsearch" data-town="Swamp Branch, KY">Search near Swamp Branch, KY</button></article></div><p class="meta">Town buttons use the regular activation search radius. They do not search along the entire trail route. Official GIS overlays for selected Kentucky routes, park trails, trailheads and campgrounds are available below; nationwide coverage remains incomplete. Official trailhead links are available for selected Kentucky trails.</p></section><div class="finder-footer"><div class="finder-footer-info"><div class="finder-footer-kicker">KENTUCKY PORTABLE CLUB</div><div class="finder-footer-tag">Get Outside. Get On The Air.</div><p>KPC Find a Park • Provided by KZ4CP</p></div><nav class="finder-footer-actions" aria-label="Quick links"><a href="parks.html">KPC Parks →</a><a href="#finder-search">Find a Park ↑</a><a href="#finder-planner">Trip Planner ↑</a><a href="resources.html">Library →</a><a href="index.html">KPC Home →</a><a href="kpc-privacy.html">Privacy</a></nav></div><footer class="finder-source">Source data: user-provided SOTA/POTA GPX and WWFF KFF–POTA cross-reference dated January 10, 2025. WWFF mapped points are inherited from linked POTA references; verify current program eligibility and boundaries. Cross-reference opportunities are marked as unverified; no confirmed double/triple activation claims are made. Distances are straight-line estimates, not driving distances. Town lookup uses OpenStreetMap Nominatim. GPS is requested only with permission; sharing a search link can include the selected coordinates.<div style="text-align:center;padding:8px 0 14px"><a href="find.html" style="color:inherit;font-weight:700">FIND IT →</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href="kpc-about-info.html" style="color:inherit;font-weight:700">ABOUT OUR INFORMATION</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href="kpc-privacy.html" style="color:inherit;font-weight:700">PRIVACY</a></div><div style="margin-top:8px;font-weight:700">KPC tools and guides are planning aids, not official sources. We make mistakes. Do your own research and check official maps. KPC is an independent ham radio club, not part of Parks on the Air&reg;, SOTA or WWFF.</div></footer><div id="kpc-rules"></div><script src="kpc-rules-card.js?v=20261018a"></script>
